<title>SRI LANKA: Ceylon Tobacco up on local buying.</title>
<headline>Ceylon Tobacco up on local buying.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ceylon Tobacco Co Ltd rose 5.3 percent or 1.5 rupees to 30 on retail buying on Friday, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The share is now down at a level where even small retailers can afford it,&quot; said a retail broker. &quot;It has good upside potential,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>A total of 3,000 shares changed hands.</p>
<p>Cylon Tobacco, Sri Lanka's monopoly cigarette maker. is a subsidiary of B.A.T Industries Plc.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
